val.f19:
I'm using generalization mode because you'll judge on unseen tasks. The split is 6 train and 2 held out, with each of the four tools still present in train. The evaluator calls an OpenAI-compatible endpoint with the candidate as the system prompt, and the endpoint, key and model come from environment variables.

```json
{
  "seed_candidate": {
    "agent_md": "You are a support agent. Use tools to help the customer. Respond with JSON {"tool": ..., "arg": ...}."
  },
  "evaluator": {
    "type": "python",
    "timeout": 60,
    "code": "import json, os, re, urllib.request

def evaluate(candidate, example):
    text = candidate if isinstance(candidate, str) else next(iter(candidate.values()), "")
    if example is None:
        example = {"input": "Where is order 1234?", "tool": "lookup_order", "arg": "1234"}
    info = {"input": example.get("input"), "expected_tool": example.get("tool"), "expected_arg": example.get("arg")}
    try:
        base = os.environ.get("OPENAI_BASE_URL", "https://api.openai.com/v1").rstrip("/")
        body = json.dumps({
            "model": os.environ.get("MODEL", "gpt-4o-mini"),
            "temperature": 0,
            "messages": [
                {"role": "system", "content": text},
                {"role": "user", "content": example["input"]},
            ],
        }).encode()
        req = urllib.request.Request(
            base + "/chat/completions", data=body,
            headers={"Content-Type": "application/json",
                     "Authorization": "Bearer " + os.environ.get("OPENAI_API_KEY", "")})
        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=30) as r:
            reply = json.loads(r.read())["choices"][0]["message"]["content"]
    except Exception as e:
        info["error"] = repr(e)
        return 0.0, info
    info["reply"] = reply
    try:
        m = re.search(r"\{.*\}", reply, re.S)
        obj = json.loads(m.group(0))
        tool = str(obj.get("tool", "")).strip()
        arg = str(obj.get("arg", "")).strip().lower()
    except Exception as e:
        info["error"] = "unparseable JSON: " + repr(e)
        info["failing_checks"] = ["valid_json"]
        return 0.0, info
    tool_ok = tool == example["tool"]
    exp_arg = str(example["arg"]).strip().lower()
    arg_ok = exp_arg in arg if arg else False
    score = (0.7 if tool_ok else 0.0) + (0.3 if (tool_ok and arg_ok) else 0.0)
    info.update({"got_tool": tool, "got_arg": arg, "tool_ok": tool_ok, "arg_ok": arg_ok,
                 "failing_checks": [c for c, ok in (("tool", tool_ok), ("arg", arg_ok)) if not ok]})
    return score, info
"
  },
  "objective": "Maximize first-tool-call accuracy (correct tool 0.7, plus correct arg 0.3 when the tool is right) on unseen customer messages. The reply must stay a single JSON object {"tool": ..., "arg": ...} with tool one of lookup_order, start_return, search_kb, escalate. Keep the instructions concise (under 300 words) and general: no hard-coded example messages or order numbers.",
  "background": "Agent instructions are used as the system prompt. The evaluator assumes an OpenAI-compatible /chat/completions endpoint, configured through OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_BASE_URL (default https://api.openai.com/v1) and MODEL (default gpt-4o-mini); temperature 0. Tool semantics inferred from the labels: lookup_order = status or tracking of an order (arg is order number); start_return = customer wants to return or exchange an item from an order (arg is order number); search_kb = general policy, product or stock questions with no specific order action (arg is a short keyword such as 'refund' or 'size'); escalate = customer asks for a human or manager, or shows repeated or unresolved frustration (arg is order number if given). Only 8 labeled examples exist, so the 6/2 train/validation split is noisy: validation scores are a rough signal. Evaluation is exact on tool and substring on arg. Preserve the JSON output format requirement.",
  "dataset": [
    {"input": "Where is order 1234?", "tool": "lookup_order", "arg": "1234"},
    {"input": "I want to return the shoes from order 77", "tool": "start_return", "arg": "77"},
    {"input": "What's your refund policy?", "tool": "search_kb", "arg": "refund"},
    {"input": "Order 9 never arrived, I want a human", "tool": "escalate", "arg": "9"},
    {"input": "Do you have size 10 in the trail runners?", "tool": "search_kb", "arg": "size"},
    {"input": "Return order 300, it's the wrong colour", "tool": "start_return", "arg": "300"}
  ],
  "valset": [
    {"input": "Track 5521 please", "tool": "lookup_order", "arg": "5521"},
    {"input": "This is the third time I'm asking about order 42, get me a manager", "tool": "escalate", "arg": "42"}
  ],
  "config": {"max_metric_calls": 80, "max_iterations": 10}
}
```

